// ---- Chapter 6: The Fool's last ride ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// On the old gallows, under a purple kite caught on the beam (the drawing come true), Rowan kills The Fool before the
// whole city. Lucian lowers his stick on purpose: a city never listens to a man in a mask, but it will listen to the
// Hero's son, and a young man who sees the face under the mask will not stop until he knows why. The mask splits; he
// gives Rowan the bitten apple back and the Judgement card ("Don't run. Your father ran."); the kite flies free. Days
// later 800 G, the Hermit and Hale's diary reach the guild. The case: the diary is a PDF with ink "blotted" over lines
// (black boxes over text that is still there) and one line scraped and rewritten (an incremental update: the first
// revision, cut at its %%EOF, still names the real city): Frosthaven. The diary names P. as Prince and the Orchard's
// council; its line about apple stems sends Rowan back to his mother's pillow five years ago. He asks Varrick one
// question, and Varrick vanishes, leaving a glove on the riverbank. A stinger at the council table sets up the sequel.

